{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>You distract the people from their work.</b> You separate and remove them from their labor — for they listen to you and expect to rest from the work. So too ״פְּרָעֵהוּ אַל תַּעֲבֹר בּוֹ״ (Proverbs 4) — remove him; and so too ״וַתִּפְרְעוּ כָל עֲצָתִי״ (ibid. 1); ״כִּי פָרֻעַ הוּא״ (Exodus 32) — removed and abhorrent." "<b>Go to your burdens.</b> Go to the labor that you have to do in your houses — but the labor of Egypt's bondage was not upon the tribe of Levi. Know this, for Moses and Aaron go and come freely (Shemot Rabbah)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:37.048019551Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}